{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1152363-skill-confusion-in-regards-to-supernatural-politics","id":1152363,"title":"Skill confusion in regards to supernatural politics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-23T19:19:58-07:00","id":1152363,"title":"Skill confusion in regards to supernatural politics","content":"I'm running a game of Forsaken 2E, and the pack's Ithaeur is trying to learn about vampire politics. Would this just use the politics skill or would he get to roll his (much higher) occult when trying to research this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18145-goatmanofcoffee","name":"Goatmanofcoffee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T20:10:04-07:00","id":1152376,"title":"","content":"That's going to depend on what we mean by &quot;learn about&quot; and &quot;research&quot; as rolled actions.<br /> <br /> In the case of understanding the politics of humanlike supernatural entities dealing among themselves in regular material space, a la vampires? It's Politics. Nothing about the process of grasping power dynamics is particularly aided or hindered by knowledge of ritual and folklore or lack thereof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T20:35:37-07:00","id":1152381,"title":"","content":"For vampiric society in general, I would be inclined to agree with @Satchel.<br /> <br /> That said, Occult would make sense for learning about the Circle and Lancea, seeing as they're occult organizations. Who knows? You might be able to find a blood spirit to let you in on what thhey're doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T00:41:27-07:00","id":1152425,"title":"","content":"On this I'm sided with Politics, even for Lancea and Circle. Occult deals with the more metaphysical sides of their existence, and maybe with the philosophies behind those Covenants. But the power structures and social interactions are clearly the purview of Politics. Even among Spirits, by the way, that can be the case sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T06:33:04-07:00","id":1152484,"title":"","content":"As I literally was asked for the same by my players on last Werewolf session, here are <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975865-2e-researching-supernaturals-in-game\">my solution to 'researching other monsters lore' problem</a>, based on <b>Silver Ladder</b> book. Your welcome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To me it's all about Occult Skill to know <i>facts</i> about particular supernatural race and it's background ( because most of it's are various cults in mortal societies ). Politics Skill is all about knowing 'who pulls the strings' in particular location - who is 'power behind the throne' or 'what rites are good to great Lancea Sanctum official'. But general 'monsters lore' is all about Occult. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975865-2e-researching-supernaturals-in-game?p=976604#post976604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">General Rule:</span></b><i><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Every supernatural being is treated as known to characters with each Success Threshold of those fact lists - unless they are high penalties on the rolls ( -3 and more ), then they are treated as known on next Occult dot. Specialty in particular kind gives information like Success Threshold higher. So Occult 1 character knows 5 success facts and Occult 3 up to 15 successes. If there are complication on Research rolls ( like with Created ), Occult 2 character knows up to 5 success lore and Occult 4 up to 15 success. But if character have Speciality, even with penalty, character knows on Occult 2 up to 10 success of lore.</span></i></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975865-2e-researching-supernaturals-in-game?p=976632#post976632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>General Rule 2:</b> <i>Mortals and Hunters have even more problems on researching truth about monsters because millennia of their misdirection and lies. Hunters from organizations need next 5 successes or 1 dot of Occult higher for each Success Threshold. Mortals from outside those groups ( Hunters included ) need twice as much. For example, to get 5 success lore Hunter from Conspiracy need 10 successes. Hunter without help will need 15 successes. Same mortal would need 20 successes to get 5 Success Threshold on Prometheans.</i><br /> <br /> And so we have vampires lore table: <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"left\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Successes</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Information</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Vampires drink blood, are allergic to sunlight and live forever. Opinions vary on the effectiveness of crosses, garlic, wooden stakes and silver and plain old bullets.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Stakes in the heart work. Crosses, garlic and other common myths are largely myth. They like to call themselves Kindred.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">15</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Sunlight, fire and slashing weaponry are most effective against vampiric opponents.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">20</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Vampires are divided into both clans \u2013 large, archetypical bloodsuckers families - and covenants made on their unlife goal with political infighting and backstabbing featuring as common events.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">25+</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Names and descriptions of the common clans and covenants are found along with minor explanations of how they interact.</td> </tr> </table></div></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T06:45:57-07:00","id":1152490,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> You'd get all that knowledge out of interrogating a ghoul in like 5 minutes. Even less considering Mind and Space arcana; but the interrogation tactic would still suffice for a forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T07:47:57-07:00","id":1152504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1152363-skill-confusion-in-regards-to-supernatural-politics?p=1152490#post1152490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> You'd get all that knowledge out of interrogating a ghoul in like 5 minutes. Even less considering Mind and Space arcana; but the interrogation tactic would still suffice for a forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Ghoul is reliable source, entreched in 'his Master's' lore. So does Wolf - Blooded know A LOT more on Uratha or Shadow Realm than random vampire or changeling. My rules assumes you look for 'What my character know about other monsters from his Occult RIGHT NOW' - If you want to know more, go roll some Research from Intelligence +Occult, to 'hit the books'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-24-2017, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T08:24:32-07:00","id":1152514,"title":"","content":"Research generally needs a volume of works to peruse. I severely doubt those are readily available to random characters, specially when they've had no other source of contact with supernatural denizens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T10:38:54-07:00","id":1152552,"title":"","content":"This is one of the things Conditions are for.<br /> <br /> If you're investigating vampire society, you can easily start with an Occult research roll, gain the Informed Condition, and cash that in on your Politics roll to grok vampire politics as your in-depth knowledge of the undead's metaphysical state makes it easier for you to unravel the intricate nuances of vampire politics.<br /> <br /> It doesn't hurt that this is how the Advanced Library Merit works: each dot is a supernatural type/phenomena and you can claim the Informed Condition about that subject once per interval, then apply it to whatever you're doing with them. Complex research rules not needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T12:02:09-07:00","id":1152576,"title":"","content":"Another option for using Occult and Politics in regards to Vampire society is to treat the Occult skill as the one used to learn information about that society and the Politics skill as the one used to actively manipulate or interpret that society.<br /> For example:<br /> \u200bOccult lets you know that the Ventrue imbed themselves within political and financial institutions, that they are nominally aligned with the Lancea who are at odds with the Circle, but Politics is the skill used when trying to leverage that knowledge to achieve a tangible result or predict how it will influence the cities power structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T15:40:40-07:00","id":1154861,"title":"","content":"The problem is what kind of information you would &quot;realistically&quot; get from lore on mysticism.<br /> <br /> On the aforementioned example, I do think that a heavy lore on Occult could reliably let you know that:<br /> - A group of Vampires called Invictus does exist;<br /> - A group of Vampires called Lancea et Sanctum does exist;<br /> - The Invictus is known for its meddling with secular power both in Undead and Mortal societies;<br /> - The Lancea et Sanctum is known as the priesthood of Roman Catholic Vampires;<br /> - Both were known as First and Second State, and had a symbiotic relationship in the past.<br /> <br /> But I don't think on Occult covering on the specifics of their nightly affairs, or in the current situation in a given city. I think about Occult as covering things that &quot;bleed&quot; in legend and lore, and on the &quot;science&quot; of the supernatural, so to speak.<br /> <br /> Politics, though, is certainly more about understanding social relations than knowing them beforehand. A character can't understand political relations without some contact with them, so it isn't feasible to know the current relation between them beforehand.<br /> <br /> In the end it is the point for me, though. There are things that shouldn't be governed by a single roll. A Werewolf that succeeds in Occult can know several things about Vampires and how they are supposed to gather. But it isn't even conceivable about such a character knowing how the Invictus works in the city without ever being in contact with the Invictus, at least indirectly. You can make the lore work as indirect contact if you want, but it isn't comprehension by itself.<br /> <br /> As for interrogating a Ghoul, or anyone, actually, you can skip absolutely any check by forcing someone who already knows it, so no big deal. You can substitute Science, Occult, Politics, Academics, Drive, and any other roll whatsoever by threatening a specialist with violence. It isn't doesn't diminish a roll just because you can punch a guy who knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}